# telemetry-honesty-safety-adjacent (2026-07-17): scripts/backup-n8n-data.mjs
# opens with a `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang. With core.autocrlf=true and no
# .gitattributes, Windows checkouts normalize the committed LF blob to CRLF
# on disk — harmless for `node` itself (it strips \r\n shebangs fine), but
# esbuild's shebang-stripping regex (used by Vite/Vitest's transform
# pipeline) does not handle a \r\n-terminated shebang and throws
# "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" at import time, breaking
# scripts/backup-n8n-data.mjs's own test suite
# (src/server/__tests__/backup-n8n-data-fail-loud.test.ts) on every fresh
# Windows checkout. Force LF for this file so the on-disk shebang always
# parses regardless of the checking-out environment's autocrlf setting.
scripts/backup-n8n-data.mjs text eol=lf

# generated-artifact honesty gate (2026-07-20): docs/cold-recovery-runsheet.md is RENDERED
# from scripts/ops/recovery-evidence.cjs, and `npm run runsheet:check` compares the file to
# a fresh render. With core.autocrlf=true and no rule here, a Windows checkout smudges the
# committed LF blob to CRLF on disk while render() emits LF — so the gate false-REDs
# "STALE or HAND-EDITED" on a pristine clone. Same class as the shebang entry above,
# reproduced one file over. CI is Linux so it never saw it; a contributor would.
docs/cold-recovery-runsheet.md text eol=lf
